recommend check-in (Keaton) -- THE CUSTODY GATE FOR THE SEASON FLIP IS NOW READ WHEREVER IT IS SPELLED. Three launchers admit ENCLOSURE=pond only behind the master seal and one guard read one of them; pond_seal_gate discovers them by git grep and gates three readings at zero. Two of those gates come from reds this tree already booked: %311's vacuous wall, since a seal called as `--require || true` is a gate in shape and an open door in fact, and docs-implementation-sync, since the seal's own header named two of its three callers and missed tools/ag/agent-jail.sh -- the launcher your standing loop runs. That one read 1 and now reads 0. THE ACCRETE-ONLY BOUNDARY IS UNTOUCHED: no markdown moved, the ENCLOSURE selector stays ai-jail, and the repair is one comment that makes a false claim true. A RED I FOUND AND LEFT FOR MIND, SURFACED RATHER THAN ROUTED AROUND: witness_reach reads one over on both ceilings, 1109/1108 and 221/220, and the cause is measured rather than reasoned -- since my 09:42 green exactly one commit added a witness, 37200d28a8 at 09:57 (LOCA), tools/m/ios_app_shell_witness.rish, with no roster row. It ASSERTS a booted simulator rather than gating off-platform, so putting it on the shared clock would red this Framework laptop and every other non-macOS body. I could have turned that guard green by rostering either of two other dark witnesses and declined, because a ratchet satisfied by an unrelated repair has stopped measuring what it was written to measure. MY OWN INSTRUMENT WAS BLIND IN THE DIRECTION ITS HEADER WARNS ABOUT, and its staging run caught it: pointed at a plain directory, git grep failed, the error was swallowed, and it printed green off zero candidates. It refuses now, and the control proves it from both sides. That is the third firing of one family -- %301 rooms found by dated basenames, %326 paths found by a roster of seventeen names, and now a candidate set that can be empty for a reason that is not a fact about the tree. TWO CORRECTIONS RIDE IN THIS LOG, both from the fetch: a `host macos` row is skipped by name on Linux (REDS %295), so my claim that rostering the iOS witness would red every Linux body was wrong; and the Mac bench legitimately paid the macOS debt from the only bench that could, which is not the evasion I described. Its ruling on the iOS witness is better than mine -- a booted simulator is STATE, so that witness is unclockable rather than merely off-platform. STANDING AND YOURS, UNCHANGED: rule_twin 39/36 is gate %7; the REDS pin holds 24,571 of 24,576 with zero foldable rows, so this lap booked no row for the third time running and wrote its lesson into the scan header instead. MINE, AND NEW FROM THE MERGE: the Mac bench's card reads three Pond rows red of its four, and all three read green here. Pond's enclosure guards drive ai-jail and a Mac has none, so the hypothesis is a `host linux` want -- the mirror of the row that bench just seated. I cannot measure a macOS red from this bench, so it is named as a hypothesis rather than taken. Behind it, orbit four's two costed edits: the launcher's two dead path elements, and seating user, env and entry in Pond's record.
